; Creatures that monster squads are made of (docs/MUTANTS.md). One [creature_<id>] per kind.
;   name                 : display name (logs, debug status)
;   form                 : Skyrim.esm leveled actor list (LVLN) or actor base (NPC_) placed when the squad comes online;
;                          a leveled list lets the engine pick the variant for the player's level, like vanilla encounters
;   health, health_per_level, damage, damage_per_level, hit : offline stats for the board (power = sqrt(damage * hit * health) * 10,
;                          the formula human members use), approximating the vanilla creatures at each level
; form = <hex FormID> for Skyrim.esm, or <plugin>|<local id hex> for a record in another plugin (resolved when the game has
; loaded; a creature whose plugin is not loaded is dropped with one log line, and squads left without creatures are never made).
;   parts                : what a hunter takes from one it kills offline (<Skyrim.esm hex form>:<count>, ...); hunters sell them
;                          to traders (activity_factions harvest_parts / hunt_lairs in alife.ltx)
; Vanilla, Dawnguard and Dragonborn creatures only; the one Creation Club exception is Plague of the Dead (zombies).

